According to a report by Intel Market Research, Global programmatic advertising market size was valued at USD 182.3 billion in 2025. The market is slated to increase from USD 190.5 billion in 2026 to USD 312.7 billion by 2034, reflecting a CAGR of about 5.9 % during the forecast period.
Programmatic advertising refers to the automated buying and selling of digital ad inventory through real time bidding platforms, data driven algorithms, and demand side or supply side exchanges. It enables advertisers to target audiences with precision while optimizing spend across display, video, mobile and connected TV channels.
